[metadata] {"type": "create", "filePath": "/workspace/repo/changelog_unreleased/typescript/pr-6521.md", "content": "#### Break long type parameters consistently in variable declarations and arrow return types ([#6521](https://github.com/prettier/prettier/pull/6521) by [@prettier](https://github.com/prettier))

When a single generic type argument contains a union, intersection, `keyof`, array (`[]`), or indexed access (`["key"]`) type that exceeds the print width, it is now broken onto its own indented line with the closing angle bracket on a new line. This behavior is applied consistently to both variable declarations and (async) arrow function return type annotations.

<!-- prettier-ignore -->
```tsx
// Input
const foo: Foo<AaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaAaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa & BbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbBbbb> = {};
export const getVehicleDescriptor = async (
  vehicleId: string,
): Promise<Collections.Parts.PrintedCircuitBoardAssembly['attributes'] | undefined> => {}

// Prettier stable
const bar: Foo<AaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaAaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa &
  BbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbBbbb> = {};
